<title>USA: U.S. Oct leading indicators +0.1 pct - Conference Bd.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct leading indicators +0.1 pct - Conference Bd.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Conference Board index of leading, coincident and lagging indicators (1987=100) and percent changes from previous months, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>    -			Index---Oct  Sept-Rev from   Aug</p>
<p> Leading Indicators    103.6   0.1    0.2   0.1     0.1</p>
<p> Coincident Indicators 121.8  -0.1    0.2   0.2     0.2</p>
<p> Lagging Indicators    102.3  -0.1   unch   0.3    -0.1</p>
<p>Following are components of the index of leading indicators with net contributions to monthly changes.</p>
<p>    -			    Oct   Sept-Rev from    Aug</p>
<p> Average Workweek	  -0.09   0.04   0.04     0.04</p>
<p> Initial Jobless Claims   0.01  -0.10  -0.10     0.07</p>
<p> Consumer Goods Orders    0.07   0.02   0.05    -0.05</p>
<p> Slower Deliveries	  0.04  -0.10  -0.10     0.05</p>
<p> Plant, Equipment Orders -0.02   0.13   0.11    -0.08</p>
<p>    -			    Oct   Sept-Rev from    Aug</p>
<p> Building Permits	  -0.04  -0.02  -0.02    -0.03</p>
<p> Unfilled Orders	    0.02  -0.06  -0.06    -0.15</p>
<p> Materials Prices	   0.04   0.12   0.11     0.16</p>
<p> Stock Prices		 0.10   0.05   0.05     0.08</p>
<p> Money Supply		 UNCH   UNCH  -0.01     0.03</p>
<p> Consumer Expectations    UNCH   0.05   0.05     0.01</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected October leading indicators to rise 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>The October advance marks the ninth straight monthly rise.</p>
</text>
